## Setting Boot Parameters

The boot service (`boot-service`, which replaces BSS from {{ provisioner_name }}
0.2 on) is what provides the path to vmlinuz and the initrd, and provides the
kernel parameters to the node during iPXE.

First check that the boot images are available.
<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment check boot-images -->
```bash
s3cmd ls -Hr s3://boot-images/
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Get some data from our images to create our boot-service payload.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Get info from image to use for boot-service -->
```bash
export s3Output=$(s3cmd ls -Hr s3://boot-images/)
export os=$(echo "$s3Output" | awk '{print $4}' | grep 'boot-images/compute')
export ramfs=$(echo "$s3Output" | awk '{print $4}' | grep 'initram')
export hdrs=$(echo "$s3Output" | awk '{print $4}' | grep 'vmlinuz')
export params="ds=nocloud-net;s=http://${sms_ip}:8081/metadata-service/ \
nomodeset ro root=live:http://${sms_ip}:9000/${os:5} ip=dhcp \
overlayroot=tmpfs overlayroot_cfgdisk=disabled apparmor=0 selinux=0 \
console=ttyS0,115200 ip6=off cloud-init=enabled"
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Create a YAML payload for boot-service. A boot configuration carries a `name`,
and the kernel, initrd, params and the MACs it applies to.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Define the boot-service payload -->
```bash
mkdir -p /opt/ohpc/admin/nodes
cat > /opt/ohpc/admin/nodes/compute-boot.yaml <<EOF
name: compute
kernel: 'http://${sms_ip}:9000/${hdrs:5}'
initrd: 'http://${sms_ip}:9000/${ramfs:5}'
params: '${params}'
macs:
EOF
for((i=0; i < $num_computes; i++)); do
	echo "  - ${c_mac[$i]}" >> \
		/opt/ohpc/admin/nodes/compute-boot.yaml
done
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

And then finally upload our payload.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Upload the boot-service payload -->
```bash
ochami -k boot config add \
	-f yaml -d @/opt/ohpc/admin/nodes/compute-boot.yaml
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
